{
  "id": "phase-rs_phase_2660",
  "repo_name": "phase-rs/phase",
  "repo_url": "https://github.com/phase-rs/phase",
  "base_commit": "779c8aaf38766e12cd57ad1d5e1c6da258eb0ed4",
  "pr_number": 2660,
  "issue_number": 2648,
  "issue_title": "[Bug]: static \"\u2026 and can't attack or block\" drops the combat lockout (CR 508.1a / 509.1b)",
  "issue_body": "## Description\nWhen a permanent's static ability is a conjunction whose **trailing** clause is \"**and can't attack or block**\", the combat lockout is silently dropped. The leading clause (a type change, an ability-loss, a P/T modifier, etc.) parses, but the \"and can't attack or block\" half produces no static, so the affected creature can still attack and block.\n\nThis is the same drop-on-conjunction class already fixed for the sibling clauses:\n- \"\u2026 and can't be blocked\" (#2167), \"\u2026 and can't block\" (#2251), \"\u2026 and can't attack\" (#2281),\n- \"\u2026 and doesn't untap during its controller's untap step\" (#2293),\n- \"\u2026 and can't be sacrificed\" (#2458), \"\u2026 and can't be enchanted [or equipped]\" (#2452),\n- \"\u2026 and can't be the target of \u2026\" (#2522), \"\u2026 and its activated abilities can't be activated\" (#2483).\n\nThe combined **\"can't attack or block\"** is the remaining gap in that family. The standalone form (\"Enchanted creature can't attack or block.\") already parses to `StaticMode::CantAttackOrBlock`, but the compound form does not: `try_split_and_cant_attack` matches \"and can't attack\" and then **deliberately declines** when a tail remains (its own comment: *\"A remaining tail \u2026 is a different restriction owned by another branch \u2014 decline so we don't mis-split it\"*), and there is no `try_split_and_cant_attack_or_block`. So the whole \"and can't attack or block\" clause falls through and is dropped.\n\nBecause the card still parses cleanly (the leading clause succeeds), these are counted as \"supported\" by the coverage metric \u2014 a silent no-op, not a parse failure.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n1. Parse a permanent whose static reads \"[some static] **and can't attack or block**\" \u2014 e.g.:\n   - **Observed Stasis** / **Fog on the Barrow-Downs** (enchanted creature is/becomes something **and can't attack or block**)\n   - **Immovable Rod** (\"another target permanent loses all abilities **and can't attack or block**\")\n   - Auras of the form \"Enchanted creature is a [type] **and can't attack or block**.\" / \"Enchanted creature loses all abilities **and can't attack or block**.\"\n2. Resolve / inspect the resulting static abilities.\n3. Only the leading static is present; there is no `CantAttackOrBlock` static \u2014 the affected creature can still be declared as an attacker and as a blocker.\n\n## Expected behavior (CR 508.1a / CR 509.1b)\n> A creature with \"can't attack\" can't be declared as an attacker (CR 508.1a); a creature with \"can't block\" can't be declared as a blocker (CR 509.1b). \"Can't attack or block\" imposes both.\n\nThe conjunction must be split: the leading clause parses to its own static(s), and \"and can't attack or block\" adds a companion `StaticMode::CantAttackOrBlock` over the same affected set (and any shared condition), exactly as the sibling split-static fixes do.\n\n## Actual behavior\nThe trailing \"and can't attack or block\" is dropped entirely; no combat-lockout static is produced, so the affected creature can attack and block normally. Half the card does nothing.\n\n## Impact\nRoughly 8 cards carry this exact compound clause (Observed Stasis, Fog on the Barrow-Downs, Immovable Rod, and the \"is a [type] / loses all abilities \u2026 and can't attack or block\" Auras). For each, the defining removal effect (a Pacifism-style combat lockout) is silently inert \u2014 a correctness gap on cards whose primary purpose is to neutralize a creature in combat.\n\n## Implementation (mirror the sibling split-static fixes)\n- **`parser/oracle_static/evasion.rs`** \u2014 add `try_split_and_cant_attack_or_block`, mirroring `try_split_and_cant_attack` / `try_split_and_cant_block`: scan for a trailing \"and can't attack or block\" (ASCII + U+2019 apostrophe), splice it out, parse the leading clause via `parse_static_line_multi`, and append a companion `StaticDefinition::new(StaticMode::CantAttackOrBlock)` over `defs[0].affected` (carrying any shared condition). Reuse the existing \"can't attack or block\" combinator (evasion.rs ~1800) that the standalone path already uses, so the combined form maps to the same mode.\n- **`parser/oracle_static/mod.rs`** \u2014 register `try_split_and_cant_attack_or_block` in the split-static dispatch list, ordered **before** `try_split_and_cant_attack` so the combined form is matched first (the bare-attack splitter already declines the tail, so this is belt-and-suspenders).\n- **Tests (`tests.rs`)** \u2014 a compound \"is a [type] and can't attack or block\" and a \"loses all abilities and can't attack or block\" each produce the leading static plus a `CantAttackOrBlock` companion sharing the affected set; the existing bare \"can't attack\" / \"can't block\" / \"can't be blocked\" splits remain unaffected.\n\nNo engine extension is required: `StaticMode::CantAttackOrBlock` already exists and is enforced.\n\n## Component\n- `crates/engine/src/parser/oracle_static/evasion.rs` \u2014 no `try_split_and_cant_attack_or_block`; `try_split_and_cant_attack` declines the \"or block\" tail.\n- `crates/engine/src/parser/oracle_static/mod.rs` \u2014 the split-static dispatch list omits the combined clause.\n\nCR 508.1a / CR 509.1b (see also the merged sibling fixes: #2167, #2251, #2281).",
